
# EXP-24: Naive Bayes Classification and Decision Tree Classification in WEKA

======================================================================
  EXPERIMENT 24: NAIVE BAYES & DECISION TREE (J48) CLASSIFICATION
======================================================================

1. OBJECTIVE:
   To construct Naive Bayes and J48 Decision Tree classifiers in WEKA for the 
   classic 'buys_computer' dataset and compare classification accuracy.

2. WEKA ARFF DATASET (buys_computer_exp24.arff):
----------------------------------------------------------------------
@relation buys_computer_dataset

@attribute age {<=30, 31..40, >40}
@attribute income {high, medium, low}
@attribute student {no, yes}
@attribute credit_rating {fair, excellent}
@attribute buys_computer {no, yes}

@data
<=30, high, no, fair, no
<=30, high, no, excellent, no
31..40, high, no, fair, yes
>40, medium, no, fair, yes
>40, low, yes, fair, yes
>40, low, yes, excellent, no
31..40, low, yes, excellent, yes
<=30, medium, no, fair, no
<=30, low, yes, fair, yes
>40, medium, yes, fair, yes
<=30, medium, yes, excellent, yes
31..40, medium, no, excellent, yes
31..40, high, yes, fair, yes
>40, medium, no, excellent, no
----------------------------------------------------------------------

3. WEKA EXECUTION STEPS:
   a. Classify tab -> Choose Classifier:
      - Naive Bayes: weka.classifiers.bayes.NaiveBayes
      - Decision Tree: weka.classifiers.trees.J48 -C 0.25 -M 2
   b. Test Options: Use training set / Cross-validation 10-fold.
   c. Click Start.

